    "Archives use private local permissions but are not encrypted remote backups; production retention, scheduling, encryption, cutover and recovery runbook acceptance remain C15 scope.",
    "Only a conservative single-poster legacy/explicit external mapping is projected; ambiguous or unsupported input remains needs_review, with original bytes preserved.",
    "Registered files, unknown paths, original intake, diagnostics and journals are never automatically pruned. Completed result verification requires the retained immutable staging plan/journal.",
    "No daily schema migration, actual legacy-history import, production GC, account provisioning, service cutover or paid remote call was performed.",
    "C12 Linux HTTPS and C12/C13 real Paddle evidence, frontend source/unit/build and legacy launchers are retained; C14 reruns default Python, full PostgreSQL core and direct/Vite browser flows."
